# Implementation Plan - Personal Portfolio & Prompt Library

Create a comprehensive personal knowledge base web app as a single standalone HTML file (using React and Tailwind CSS) to capture skills, projects, work experience, ideas, and education, featuring an AI-powered prompt library.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Single File Deliverable**: The PRD specifies a single standalone HTML file. For development, I will use a Vite-based workflow for better organization and then provide a build step that outputs a single HTML file using `vite-plugin-singlefile`. Does this workflow work for you, or should I write directly into one large HTML file?

> [!WARNING]
> **Prompt Generation**: The PRD mentions "Claude API via fetch". Note that calling the Claude API directly from the frontend (client-side) will expose your API key. Usually, this requires a proxy or backend. For a "no-backend" app, we might need to instruct the user on how to handle this safely or use a client-side key input (stored in localStorage).

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Project Setup & Foundation
- Initialize a React project using Vite.
- Configure Tailwind CSS with the specified color palette (`#1A1A2E`, `#6C63FF`, `#00B4A6`).
- Set up the main layout with a 3-tab navigation system.

### Phase 2: State & Storage
- Implement a robust `usePortfolio` hook or context to manage the global state.
- Set up `localStorage` synchronization for all 5 categories + custom prompts.
- Define the data schema based on the PRD.

### Phase 3: Portfolio Tab
- **Stats Bar**: Component to display counts for each category.
- **Search & Filter**: Implementation of the search bar and category toggle chips.
- **Timeline View**: Vertical timeline component with preview cards.
- **Entry Modals**: Dynamic modal system for viewing, adding, and editing entries across all 5 categories.

### Phase 4: Prompt Library Tab
- **Prompt Generator**: Logic to select categories and fill template variables.
- **Templates**: Hardcode the predefined templates for Projects, Skills, and Work.
- **Custom Prompts**: CRUD functionality for user-defined prompts.
- **Copy Logic**: "Copy to clipboard" functionality for generated prompts.

### Phase 5: Settings Tab
- **Data Management**: Export to JSON and CSV.
- **Import Logic**: File upload and data merging/overwriting.
- **Clear All**: Confirmation modal and state reset.

### Phase 6: Final Polish & Single-File Build
- Apply the full design system (Dark mode, glassmorphism, rounded corners).
- Optimize for performance (e.g., memoization for the timeline).
- Configure `vite-plugin-singlefile` to bundle everything into `index.html`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Unit tests for data export/import logic.
- UI verification using the browser tool to ensure tab switching and modal interactions work.

### Manual Verification
- Test `localStorage` persistence by refreshing the page after adding entries.
- Verify JSON/CSV exports by opening them in a text editor/spreadsheet tool.
- Test search and filtering responsiveness.
